%N A244839 Decimal expansion of the Euler double sum Sum_{m>0}(Sum_{n>0}((-1)^(m+n-1)/((2*m-1)*(m+n-1)^3))) (negated).
%C A244839 The computation of this constant is given by Bailey and Borwein as an example of the use of CAS packages to check digital integrity of published mathematics.
%H A244839 Vincenzo Librandi, <a href="/A244839/b244839.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..1000</a>
%H A244839 David H. Bailey and Jonathan M. Borwein, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-21473-3_3">Experimental computation as an ontological game changer</a>, in: Ernest Davis and Philip J. Davis (eds.), Mathematics, Substance and Surmise, Springer Cham, 2015, pp. 25-67; <a href="https://www.davidhbailey.com/dhbpapers/ontology.pdf">alternative link</a>. See p. 4.
%H A244839 J. M. Borwein, I. J. Zucker, and J. Boersma, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s11139-007-9083-z">The evaluation of character Euler double sums</a>, The Ramanujan Journal, Volume 15, Issue 3 (April 2008), pp. 377-405; <a href="https://carmamaths.org/resources/jon/bzb7.pdf">alternative link</a>. See p. 17.
%H A244839 Anthony Sofo and Amrik Singh Nimbran, <a href="https://doi.org/10.3390/math7090833">Euler sums and integral connections</a>, Mathematics, Vol. 7, No. 9 (2019), Article 833. See p. 12.
%H A244839 Eric Weisstein's MathWorld, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Polylogarithm.html">Polylogarithm</a>.
%H A244839 <a href="/index/Ha#harmonic">Index entries for sequences related to harmonic numbers</a>.
%F A244839 Equals 4*polylog(4, 1/2) - (151/2880)*Pi^4 - (Pi^2/6)*log(2)^2 + (1/6)*log(2)^4 + (7/2)*log(2)*zeta(3).
%F A244839 Equals -Sum_{k>=1} (-1)^(k+1) * O(k)/k^3, where O(k) = A350669(k)/A350670(k) is the k-th odd harmonic number (or harmonic number of the second kind) (Sofo and Nimbran, 2019). - _Amiram Eldar_, Sep 04 2026
%e A244839 -0.87292928952035451895794199102873253738299452053432445689371621121704773167...
%t A244839 4*PolyLog[4, 1/2] - 151/2880*Pi^4 - Pi^2/6*Log[2]^2 + 1/6*Log[2]^4 + 7/2*Log[2]*Zeta[3] // RealDigits[#, 10, 105]& // First
%o A244839 (PARI) 151*Pi^4/2880 + Pi^2*log(2)^2/6 - 4*polylog(4, 1/2) - log(2)^4/6 - 7*log(2)*zeta(3)/2 \\ _Charles R Greathouse IV_, Aug 27 2014
